d an Assistant Professor of Public Policy at the \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://www.hks.harvard.edu/faculty/stephen-casper\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"Harvard Kennedy School\"]]],[5,\" and a Faculty Affiliate of the Harvard School of Engineering and Applied Sciences. Prior to joining Harvard, he completed his PhD at MIT and did a research residency with the UK AI Security Institute. He is a writer for the International AI Safety Report and a lead writer for the Singapore Consensus. His talk, “Predicting the first major AI-enabled terrorism incident: A pre-mortem and 9 predictions”: \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://luma.com/ai-incident-response-sprint-stephen-casper\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"RSVP for Friday, September 11 at 2:00 PM ET\"]]],[5,\".\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":220},"stephen-casper-air26",{"type":6,"value":45},{"wQtXmT0fg":223,"t79s88Zpi":229,"MW9jJHDjl":231,"hZUKo6j_C":233,"MKXxFl3jj":234,"nAGf_p8u2":237,"id":239},{"type":11,"value":224},{"src":225,"srcSet":226,"pixelWidth":227,"pixelHeight":228},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/8Th9zvgti3mVF9ERyx5wufyLAF8.jpg?width=1004&height=987","https://framerusercontent.com/images/8Th9zvgti3mVF9ERyx5wufyLAF8.jpg?scale-down-to=512&width=1004&height=987 512w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/8Th9zvgti3mVF9ERyx5wufyLAF8.jpg?width=1004&height=987 1004w",1004,987,{"type":117,"value":230},"https://davidscottkrueger.com/",{"type":6,"value":232},"David Krueger",{"type":6,"value":214},{"type":27,"value":235},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":236},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"David is the CEO of \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://evitable.com/\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"Evitable\"]]],[5,\" and an Assistant Professor in Robust, Reasoning, and Responsible AI at the University of Montreal, and a Core Academic Member at Mila, the Quebec Artificial Intelligence Institute. He is the holder of a CIFAR AI Chair and the IVADO Professorship in Responsible AI. David's work focuses on reducing societal-scale risks from AI, such as the risks of human extinction and gradual disempowerment. \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://luma.com/ai-incident-response-sprint-david-krueger\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"RSVP for his talk on Friday, September 11 at 3:15 PM ET\"]]],[5,\".\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":238},"david-krueger-air26",{"type":6,"value":47},{"wQtXmT0fg":241,"t79s88Zpi":247,"MW9jJHDjl":249,"hZUKo6j_C":251,"MKXxFl3jj":252,"nAGf_p8u2":255,"id":257},{"type":11,"value":242},{"src":243,"srcSet":244,"pixelWidth":245,"pixelHeight":246},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/gSUxgUiyLWDJRaW6qVH4DS8HcyI.jpg?width=1572&height=1464","https://framerusercontent.com/images/gSUxgUiyLWDJRaW6qVH4DS8HcyI.jpg?scale-down-to=512&width=1572&height=1464 512w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/gSUxgUiyLWDJRaW6qVH4DS8HcyI.jpg?scale-down-to=1024&width=1572&height=1464 1024w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/gSUxgUiyLWDJRaW6qVH4DS8HcyI.jpg?width=1572&height=1464 1572w",1572,1464,{"type":117,"value":248},"https://timhua.me/",{"type":6,"value":250},"Tim Hua",{"type":6,"value":214},{"type":27,"value":253},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":254},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Tim Hua is a member of technical staff at \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://metr.org/\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"METR\"]]],[5,\", working on alignment assessments and evaluations, and speaks here in a personal capacity. He was previously at Transluce studying model behaviours, an Astra Fellow with Redwood Research, and a MATS scholar under Neel Nanda and Sam Marks. His recent work includes steering evaluation-aware models to act like they are deployed, and combining cost-constrained runtime monitors for AI safety. \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://luma.com/ai-incident-response-sprint-tim-hua\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"RSVP for his talk on Friday, September 11 at 5:15 PM PT\"]]],[5,\".\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":256},"tim-hua-air26",{"type":6,"value":49},{"wQtXmT0fg":259,"t79s88Zpi":267,"MW9jJHDjl":269,"hZUKo6j_C":271,"MKXxFl3jj":272,"nAGf_p8u2":275,"id":277},{"type":11,"value":260},{"src":261,"positionX":262,"positionY":263,"srcSet":264,"pixelWidth":265,"pixelHeight":266},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/Pc5qHdx3oErfwxjVQc0Fm6ijASQ.webp?width=800&height=1021","42.5%","22.4%","https://framerusercontent.com/images/Pc5qHdx3oErfwxjVQc0Fm6ijASQ.webp?width=800&height=1021 800w",800,1021,{"type":117,"value":268},"https://www.linkedin.com/in/henry-papadatos/",{"type":6,"value":270},"Henry Papadatos",{"type":6,"value":214},{"type":27,"value":273},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":274},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Henry Papadatos is the Executive Director of \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://www.safer-ai.org/\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"SaferAI\"]]],[5,\", where he works on technical solutions for frontier AI risk management. He contributed to the EU AI Act's Codes of Practice as part of the expert working group on risk taxonomy and assessment, and helped draft the G7 Hiroshima AI Process reporting framework through the OECD task force. His technical work includes an AI risk management ratings system for developers and current research on quantitative risk modeling for AI-enabled cyber threats. Before SaferAI, he conducted alignment research on large language models at UC Berkeley's Center for Human-Compatible AI. \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://luma.com/ai-incident-response-sprint-henry-papadatos\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"RSVP for his talk on Friday, September 11 at 3:15 PM CEST\"]]],[5,\".\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":276},"henry-papadatos-air26",{"type":6,"value":51},{"wQtXmT0fg":279,"t79s88Zpi":283,"MW9jJHDjl":285,"hZUKo6j_C":287,"MKXxFl3jj":288,"nAGf_p8u2":291,"id":293},{"type":11,"value":280},{"src":281,"pixelWidth":282,"pixelHeight":282},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/QunZDfM0q2UIGsYPlZ5Arn6MB0.jpg?width=400&height=400",400,{"type":117,"value":284},"https://github.com/AlexTMallen",{"type":6,"value":286},"Alex Mallen",{"type":6,"value":214},{"type":27,"value":289},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":290},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Alex Mallen is a Member of Technical Staff at \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://www.redwoodresearch.org/\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"Redwood Research\"]]],[5,\", where he works on AI safety. He has worked on scalable oversight, AI evaluations, eliciting latent knowledge, interpretability, and AI control. He studied CS at the University of Washington and previously worked at EleutherAI. His talk, “How near-term AI swarms could cause labs to lose control of AI development, absent improved defenses”: \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://luma.com/ai-incident-response-sprint-alex-mallen\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"RSVP for Friday, September 11 at 2:15 PM PT\"]]],[5,\".\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":292},"alex-mallen-air26",{"type":6,"value":53},{"wQtXmT0fg":295,"t79s88Zpi":300,"MW9jJHDjl":302,"hZUKo6j_C":304,"MKXxFl3jj":305,"nAGf_p8u2":308,"id":310},{"type":11,"value":296},{"src":297,"srcSet":298,"pixelWidth":83,"pixelHeight":299},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/GYKKi3a2gJ7p3tRTxif3BUth34.jpg?width=868&height=1097","https://framerusercontent.com/images/GYKKi3a2gJ7p3tRTxif3BUth34.jpg?scale-down-to=1024&width=868&height=1097 810w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/GYKKi3a2gJ7p3tRTxif3BUth34.jpg?width=868&height=1097 868w",1097,{"type":117,"value":301},"https://ailab.ijs.si/marko_grobelnik/",{"type":6,"value":303},"Marko Grobelnik",{"type":6,"value":214},{"type":27,"value":306},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":307},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Marko Grobelnik is a researcher in the field of Artificial Intelligence (AI). Focused areas of expertise are Machine Learning, Data/Text/Web Mining, Network Analysis, Semantic Technologies, Deep Text Understanding, and Data Visualization. Marko co-leads Artificial Intelligence Lab at \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://ailab.ijs.si/\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"Jozef Stefan Institute\"]]],[5,\", cofounded UNESCO International Research Center on AI (IRCAI), and is the CEO of Quintelligence.com specialized in solving complex AI tasks for the commercial world. Marko represents Slovenia in OECD AI Committee (AIGO/ONEAI), in Council of Europe Committee on AI (CAHAI/CAI), NATO (DARB), and Global Partnership on AI (GPAI). In 2016 Marko became Digital Champion of Slovenia at European Commission. Talk time to be confirmed: \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://luma.com/ai-incident-response-sprint-marko-grobelnik\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"RSVP to get the update\"]]],[5,\".\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":309},"marko-grobelnik-air26",{"type":6,"value":55},{"wQtXmT0fg":312,"t79s88Zpi":316,"MW9jJHDjl":318,"hZUKo6j_C":320,"MKXxFl3jj":321,"nAGf_p8u2":324,"id":326},{"type":11,"value":313},{"src":314,"srcSet":315,"pixelWidth":265,"pixelHeight":265},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/IWge8LppdQJSP8fD4suIUVa5qy0.jpg?width=800&height=800","https://framerusercontent.com/images/IWge8LppdQJSP8fD4suIUVa5qy0.jpg?scale-down-to=512&width=800&height=800 512w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/IWge8LppdQJSP8fD4suIUVa5qy0.jpg?width=800&height=800 800w",{"type":117,"value":317},"https://boydkane.com/",{"type":6,"value":319},"Boyd Kane",{"type":6,"value":214},{"type":27,"value":322},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":323},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Boyd is a technical AI safety researcher in the \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://www.matsprogram.org/\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"MATS\"]]],[5,\" 9 Extension, working with Alex Turner (Google DeepMind) and Alex Cloud (Anthropic) on methods to detect deceptively misaligned AI. He previously wrote embedded software for satellites at CubeSpace, interned at AWS in Cape Town, and holds an MSc in Computer Science from Stellenbosch University. His talk, “Uncovering public traces of the OpenAI Huggingface incident”: \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://luma.com/ai-incident-response-sprint-boyd-kane\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"RSVP for Friday, September 11 at 10:15 AM ET\"]]],[5,\".\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":325},"boyd-kane-air26",{"type":6,"value":57},{"wQtXmT0fg":328,"t79s88Zpi":334,"MW9jJHDjl":336,"hZUKo6j_C":338,"MKXxFl3jj":339,"nAGf_p8u2":342,"id":344},{"type":11,"value":329},{"src":330,"srcSet":331,"pixelWidth":332,"pixelHeight":333},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/ezZC61cgpuP3t4Rvl7FSgzPCwPU.jpg?width=861&height=724","https://framerusercontent.com/images/ezZC61cgpuP3t4Rvl7FSgzPCwPU.jpg?scale-down-to=512&width=861&height=724 512w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/ezZC61cgpuP3t4Rvl7FSgzPCwPU.jpg?width=861&height=724 861w",861,724,{"type":117,"value":335},"https://isaakmengesha.com/",{"type":6,"value":337},"Isaak Mengesha",{"type":6,"value":214},{"type":27,"value":340},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":341},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Isaak Mengesha is a researcher working on the economics and governance of technological transitions, currently focused on transformative AI. He is a postdoc at the \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://www.oxfordmartin.ox.ac.uk/\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"Oxford Martin School\"]]],[5,\"'s Programme on Forecasting Technological Change, working with the Institute for New Economic Thinking on how technologies diffuse and how to anticipate their large-scale impacts. He completed his PhD at the University of Amsterdam on the structure of economic development and technological transitions, and led research at Arcadia Impact's AI Governance Taskforce on AI incident monitoring and crisis preparedness. His talk, “Incident Response Has a Measurement Problem”: \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://luma.com/ai-incident-response-sprint-isaak-mengesha\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"RSVP for Friday, September 11 at 1:00 PM ET\"]]],[5,\".\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":343},"isaak-mengesha-air26",{"type":6,"value":59},{"wQtXmT0fg":346,"t79s88Zpi":351,"MW9jJHDjl":353,"hZUKo6j_C":355,"MKXxFl3jj":356,"nAGf_p8u2":359,"id":361},{"type":11,"value":347},{"src":348,"srcSet":349,"pixelWidth":350,"pixelHeight":350},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/DL4lpJfM1DqupO5SQ3ngWCgzhew.jpg?width=593&height=593","https://framerusercontent.com/images/DL4lpJfM1DqupO5SQ3ngWCgzhew.jpg?scale-down-to=512&width=593&height=593 512w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/DL4lpJfM1DqupO5SQ3ngWCgzhew.jpg?width=593&height=593 593w",593,{"type":117,"value":352},"https://linkedin.com/in/justinshenk",{"type":6,"value":354},"Justin Shenk",{"type":6,"value":214},{"type":27,"value":357},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":358},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Justin Shenk is an independent AI safety researcher based in Berlin. He researches mechanistic interpretability of LLMs, leads course cohorts for \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://bluedot.org/\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"BlueDot Impact\"]]],[5,\"'s AGI Strategy and Technical AI Safety courses, and organizes AI Salon Berlin, which bridges technical AI research and discussions about social values. He holds a PhD in computational neuroscience and previously co-founded the computer vision startup VisioLab. \"],[2,{\"href\":\"https://luma.com/ai-incident-response-sprint-justin-shenk\",\"openInNewTab\":false,\"smoothScroll\":false,\"relValues\":[],\"motionChild\":true,\"nodeId\":\"YKp4nbb6P\",\"scopeId\":\"contentManagement\"},[4,\"a\",null,[5,\"RSVP for his talk on Thursday, September 10 at 4:15 PM CEST\"]]],[5,\".\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":360},"justin-shenk-air26",{"type":6,"value":61},{"wQtXmT0fg":363,"t79s88Zpi":366,"MW9jJHDjl":368,"hZUKo6j_C":370,"MKXxFl3jj":372,"nAGf_p8u2":375,"id":377},{"type":11,"value":364},{"src":365,"pixelWidth":282,"pixelHeight":282},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/IAP2vPIO3dU9BEKJg7iQKsHpXSI.jpg?width=400&height=400",{"type":117,"value":367},"https://uk.linkedin.com/in/twm-stone",{"type":6,"value":369},"Twm Stone",{"type":6,"value":371},"Judge",{"type":27,"value":373},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":374},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"With a background in software engineering, Twm has experience in the threat modelling, formal verification and red teaming of AI systems. He is currently a MATS 9.1 extension fellow as part of the security stream.\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":376},"twm-stone-sps-26",{"type":6,"value":63},{"wQtXmT0fg":379,"t79s88Zpi":387,"MW9jJHDjl":389,"hZUKo6j_C":391,"MKXxFl3jj":392,"nAGf_p8u2":395,"id":397},{"type":11,"value":380},{"src":381,"positionX":382,"positionY":383,"srcSet":384,"pixelWidth":385,"pixelHeight":386},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/1ip7CXs7dtwGVbpDorE71DMJkg.png?width=864&height=1184","46.1%","85.8%","https://framerusercontent.com/images/1ip7CXs7dtwGVbpDorE71DMJkg.png?scale-down-to=1024&width=864&height=1184 747w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/1ip7CXs7dtwGVbpDorE71DMJkg.png?width=864&height=1184 864w",864,1184,{"type":117,"value":388},"https://www.linkedin.com/in/nikhil-reddy-pallepati/",{"type":6,"value":390},"Nikhil R. Pallepati",{"type":6,"value":371},{"type":27,"value":393},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":394},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Nikhil R. Pallepati is a Machine Learning Engineer at Microsoft, where he leads the design of production-scale AI systems including graph neural network-based detection systems and agentic LLM pipelines protecting Azure cloud infrastructure, with prior experience building enterprise ML systems at various Fortune 500 companies.\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":396},"nikhil-r-pallepati-sps-26",{"type":6,"value":65},{"wQtXmT0fg":399,"t79s88Zpi":405,"MW9jJHDjl":407,"hZUKo6j_C":409,"MKXxFl3jj":410,"nAGf_p8u2":413,"id":415},{"type":11,"value":400},{"src":401,"srcSet":402,"pixelWidth":403,"pixelHeight":404},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/IYTNKBGVKbQxupEc71tUy48kgk.jpg?width=3523&height=4965","https://framerusercontent.com/images/IYTNKBGVKbQxupEc71tUy48kgk.jpg?scale-down-to=1024&width=3523&height=4965 726w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/IYTNKBGVKbQxupEc71tUy48kgk.jpg?scale-down-to=2048&width=3523&height=4965 1453w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/IYTNKBGVKbQxupEc71tUy48kgk.jpg?scale-down-to=4096&width=3523&height=4965 2906w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/IYTNKBGVKbQxupEc71tUy48kgk.jpg?width=3523&height=4965 3523w",3523,4965,{"type":117,"value":406},"linkedin.com/in/kulkarniamey/",{"type":6,"value":408},"Amey Kulkarni",{"type":6,"value":371},{"type":27,"value":411},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":412},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Amey Kulkarni is a Senior Data Engineer at Walmart with deep experience building large-scale data infrastructure (Spark, Kafka, BigQuery, Kubernetes on GCP). He is the author of Context Change Impact Analysis (CCIA), a framework for governing AI agent behavior through structured context versioning, and maintains its open-source reference implementation, ctxwitch. He brings a production-engineering perspective to questions of AI system integrity, provenance, and oversight.\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":414},"amey-kulkarni-sl26",{"type":6,"value":67},{"wQtXmT0fg":417,"t79s88Zpi":422,"MW9jJHDjl":424,"hZUKo6j_C":426,"MKXxFl3jj":427,"nAGf_p8u2":430,"id":432},{"type":11,"value":418},{"src":419,"srcSet":420,"pixelWidth":421,"pixelHeight":421},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/WCC3cvgfBoDPwrg6unYL2DcbqYs.jpg?width=862&height=862","https://framerusercontent.com/images/WCC3cvgfBoDPwrg6unYL2DcbqYs.jpg?scale-down-to=512&width=862&height=862 512w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/WCC3cvgfBoDPwrg6unYL2DcbqYs.jpg?width=862&height=862 862w",862,{"type":117,"value":423},"https://linkedin.com/in/vkarthyk",{"type":6,"value":425},"Ved K",{"type":6,"value":371},{"type":27,"value":428},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":429},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Senior Security Detection Engineer at Databricks, leading the company's Kubernetes detection program, insider threat tooling, and Terraform-managed logging infrastructure. His expertise includes multi-cloud threat detection, scalable detection platforms, and behavioral anomaly detection.\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":431},"ved-k-sl26",{"type":6,"value":69},{"wQtXmT0fg":434,"t79s88Zpi":437,"MW9jJHDjl":439,"hZUKo6j_C":441,"MKXxFl3jj":442,"nAGf_p8u2":445,"id":447},{"type":11,"value":435},{"src":436,"pixelWidth":282,"pixelHeight":282},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/bzyQTbf025FQxx1GnWGi7UfX7SU.jpeg?width=400&height=400",{"type":117,"value":438},"https://linkedin.com/in/spurthitallam",{"type":6,"value":440},"Spurthi Tallam",{"type":6,"value":371},{"type":27,"value":443},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":444},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Spurthi is a senior machine learning engineer with seven years across research and production ML, currently building data, AI/ML systems at LePrix. She previously worked on LLM-powered conversational systems at Good Inside and on data and machine learning at Samsung Research, and holds an MS in Computer Science from UMass Amherst.\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":446},"spurthi-tallam-dm26",{"type":6,"value":71},{"wQtXmT0fg":449,"t79s88Zpi":40,"MW9jJHDjl":454,"hZUKo6j_C":456,"MKXxFl3jj":457,"nAGf_p8u2":460,"id":462},{"type":11,"value":450},{"src":451,"srcSet":452,"pixelWidth":453,"pixelHeight":453},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/tdTaxWDFxRB7S1e8zejpwAzYs.png?width=1254&height=1254","https://framerusercontent.com/images/tdTaxWDFxRB7S1e8zejpwAzYs.png?scale-down-to=512&width=1254&height=1254 512w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/tdTaxWDFxRB7S1e8zejpwAzYs.png?scale-down-to=1024&width=1254&height=1254 1024w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/tdTaxWDFxRB7S1e8zejpwAzYs.png?width=1254&height=1254 1254w",1254,{"type":6,"value":455},"Tim Schipper",{"type":6,"value":371},{"type":27,"value":458},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":459},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Tim Schipper is a Senior Full Stack Developer, AI Consultant, and AI Evangelist at Yielder with over 30 years of experience. He specializes in building data-intensive platforms and helping teams integrate AI tools effectively into production environments.\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":461},"tim-schipper-air-26",{"type":6,"value":73},{"wQtXmT0fg":464,"t79s88Zpi":40,"MW9jJHDjl":468,"hZUKo6j_C":470,"MKXxFl3jj":471,"nAGf_p8u2":474,"id":476},{"type":11,"value":465},{"src":466,"srcSet":467,"pixelWidth":265,"pixelHeight":265},"https://framerusercontent.com/images/8gHT6R9pfys55FbiXEv8penTI.jpg?width=800&height=800","https://framerusercontent.com/images/8gHT6R9pfys55FbiXEv8penTI.jpg?scale-down-to=512&width=800&height=800 512w,https://framerusercontent.com/images/8gHT6R9pfys55FbiXEv8penTI.jpg?width=800&height=800 800w",{"type":6,"value":469},"Kevin Wei",{"type":6,"value":371},{"type":27,"value":472},{"collectionId":217,"pointer":473},"[1,[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Kevin Wei (he/they) is a researcher at the Centre for the Governance of AI (GovAI), where they work on ensuring that advanced AI is developed and governed safely. Specifically, Kevin's research agenda is focused on the science of AI evaluations, legal AI safety/alignment, and technical AI governance/law, with peer-reviewed publications on these topics appearing in ICML, TMLR, and other top AI/AI ethics venues.\"]],[4,\"p\",{\"dir\":\"auto\"},[5,\"Kevin is also affiliated with the Oxford Martin School AI Governance Initiative and the RAND Center for AI, Security, and Technology; they were previously a Visiting Research Scientist on the UK AI Security Institute's science of evaluations team, a Fellow at RAND, and a program manager at a cloud company. They received a J.D. from Harvard Law School, a Master's in Global Affairs from Tsinghua University (where they were a Schwarzman Scholar), an M.S. in Machine Learning from Georgia Tech, and a B.A. in Mathematics-Statistics & Economics from Columbia University.\"]]]",{"type":6,"value":475},"kevin-wei-air26",{"type":6,"value":75},["Map"]]</script><div id="svg-templates" style="position: absolute; overflow: hidden; bottom: 0; left: 0; width: 0; height: 0; z-index: 0; contain: strict" aria-hidden="true">
